    ("v373_ftransfer_relic", "FR.RELIC.SOLVE.01 (Track 3, F_transfer): the axion relic from the FINITE-T misalignment ODE -- promotes experiments/ftransfer/axion_relic and DECIDES the two TFPT angle branches, replacing the v326 adiabatic toy. f_a=M_scal/128~2.4e11 GeV, m_a~23.8 ueV, lattice chi(T) n=8.16. [I] candidate scales fixed by the determinant-line atoms (128=2 dim S^+ |mu4|). [C] the frozen SPINE angle 3pi/5=108deg=pi N_fam/g_car gives Omega_a h^2~0.12 in [0.08,0.16] (lands on Omega_DM untuned) -- the robust dominant-DM branch. [X] the HILLTOP 170deg over-produces (~5.4x) -- disfavoured/fine-tuned. [X] kill: a finite-T solve robustly outside [0.08,0.16] for the spine across chi(T)/g_* would drop the dominant axion-DM branch. Stays [C]/[X] (lattice chi(T) input). Python (numpy+scipy)."),
