    ("v477_entropic_scaleflow", "GRAV.ENTROPIC.SCALEFLOW.01: the scale-flow representation of the entropic action -- v475's surviving interpretation 3 (KMS-spectral renormalisation) typed PRECISELY: the (72/17)(8 pi)^9 gap collapses to ONE moment condition on the scale weight, whose value is the SAME KMS moment TFPT already fixes (v36 f0 <-> M^2 = c3^7 Mbar^2). Zero new dials; still [C]; nothing closes. [E] SCALE-FLOW IDENTITY: -ln a = int dt/t (e^{-ta} - e^{-t}) (symbolic exact) = 2 int dchi/chi (e^{-a/chi^2} - e^{-1/chi^2}) (t = 1/chi^2, 1e-20 quadrature) -- Bianconi's log action IS the FLAT scale-integral of relative heat-kernel actions; TFPT's S_rel,chi evaluates ONE KMS scale with a weight: the bridge is a choice of SCALE MEASURE. [E] MOMENT DICTIONARY: with a weight w(t) dt/t the max-symmetric expansion gives 3 beta R mu1 + (17/24) beta^2 R^2 mu2 (mu1 = int w e^-t dt, mu2 = int w t e^-t dt); the flat weight has mu1 = mu2 = 1 = the v475 raw coefficients -- the raw action is the unit-moment point of a moment family. [E] THE ONE MOMENT CONDITION: EH pin beta' mu1 = c3/6 => m^2 = (4608 pi^2/17)(mu1^2/mu2) Mbar^2; demanding m^2 = c3^7 Mbar^2 forces EXACTLY mu2/mu1^2 = (72/17)(8 pi)^9 -- the v475 kill-test number IS a moment ratio; closure identity (4608 pi^2/17)/((72/17)(8 pi)^9) = c3^7 IDENTICALLY -- the 13 orders are a scale-measure datum, not a bridge mismatch. [E] v36 CONSISTENCY: f0 = 6(4 pi)^2/c3^7 <=> M^2/Mbar^2 = c3^7 -- same mass, two parametrisations, zero new dials. [C] consistency not derivation (the KMS weight is TFPT input; the entropic action supplies Einstein + Lambda and the FORM, TFPT the measure); negative side-record: the exact lattice-BW commutator attempt for AP2 (Peschel-Eisler simple forms) did NOT hold on the half-filled open chain (kept out, logged). [O] unchanged. Exact (sympy + one quadrature, Wolfram-mirrored)."),
    ("v478_entropic_continuum_legs", "GRAV.ENTROPIC.LEGS.01: first computable steps on the TWO remaining research legs of the entropic-action bridge (v473-v477). LEG A (AP2 continuum): the state-side modular Hamiltonian of the compressed critical state flows to the CHM/Bisognano-Wichmann geometric form -- exactly the object TFPT's Einstein derivation consumes (v323/v358). [N] Calabrese-Cardy: S(L) = (c/3) ln L + k with c_est = 1.00089/1.00038/1.00021 (pairs (8,16)/(12,24)/(16,32), monotone -> Dirac c = 1 = 2 Majoranas x 1/2, the v450 reading); gapped control c_est ~ 6e-8 (area law). [N] CHM parabola: the NN couplings of K = ln((1-C_A)/C_A) organise on beta(x) = x(L-x)/L with corr 0.866 -> 0.967 -> 0.986 (L = 8/16/24), mid-plateau drift shrinking; constants deliberately NOT asserted (lattice EH only asymptotically local). [N] quasi-locality: even-range bands vanish identically (particle-hole; max |K_{i,i+2}| ~ 1e-36), odd tail 1.8% and parabola-enveloped -- the lattice shadow of the local boost. LEG B (the measure): [E] single-scale corollary -- dmu = delta(t-t0) dt gives mu2/mu1^2 = e^{t0} exactly, so the v477 condition forces t0 = ln(72/17) + 9 ln(8 pi) = 30.461 (one dimensionless KMS time, exact closed form); DECLINED: t0 != h(E8) = 30 (difference 0.461, near-miss rejected per the v354/v355 no-free-pattern rule); deriving the measure stays OPEN. [C] the meeting point (state-side reading meets TFPT's geometric modular input in the continuum); [O] both legs open, no marker moves. High-precision numerical (mpmath 50 digits) + one exact corollary; Python-only by nature."),
    ("v479_kronheimer_quiver_bridge", "SEAM.KRONHEIMER.01: the R3 'combinatorial-to-geometric bridge' of the det K = 1 keystone (SEAM.DETK.01/v344 -- 'the rewrite attractor graph IS the du Val singularity') is an ESTABLISHED THEOREM: Kronheimer's ALE hyper-Kaehler quotient construction + Torelli classification (J. Diff. Geom. 29 (1989) 665 and 685), with ALL finite input data already TFPT compiler outputs. [E] MARKS = NULL = PERRON: C_aff delta = 0 and A delta = 2 delta on the affine-E8 McKay graph; multiset {1,2,2,3,3,4,4,5,6} = 2I irrep dims = the v312 rewrite-attractor Perron vector. [E] KRONHEIMER DIMENSION COUNT: dim_R M - 4 dim_R G = 4(sum_edges d_i d_j - sum d_i^2 + 1) = 4 -- the hyper-Kaehler quotient of the marks quiver is 4-real-dimensional (the C^2/Gamma geometry); sum_edges d_i d_j = sum d_i^2 = 120 forced by the null-vector identity. [E] GAUGE DATUM = |2I|: sum delta_i^2 = 120 = |mu4| h(E8) = 4*30, h(E8) = 30 = |Z2| N_fam g_car. [E] RESOLUTION DATA: 8 = rank(E8) exceptional spheres, intersection form -Cartan(E8) with det = 1 and SNF = identity (the Poincare-sphere link = the det K = 1 face, v232/v344); deformation space h (x) R^3, dim 24. [C] the theorems are CITED, not re-proved (same import class as NPW26/MMST/AGT, v424/v336/v459). [O] the residual premise TRANSFORMS, it does not vanish: 'the raw seam supplies ALE hyper-Kaehler data asymptotic to the (2,3,5) cone' = the SAME single arrow as SEAM.EQUIV.01 (v346 L2); no gate closes. Exact (sympy; Wolfram mirror added, counted with the verified 2026-07-21 engine run)."),
    ("v480_multilocal_four_interval", "QGEO.MULTILOCAL.01: the four mu4 marks make the seam circle a FOUR-INTERVAL free-fermion geometry -- the class whose multi-interval modular theory is EXACTLY KNOWN (Casini-Huerta mixing term; Longo-Xu multi-interval subfactors; Rehren-Tedesco multilocal fermions; KLM: holomorphic <=> trivial multi-interval inclusion, mu = 1 -- the SAME one bit as det K = 1). The bedrock invariance omega o rho = omega (QGEO.SYM.01) exhibited MANIFEST at the 4-interval state level on the exactly solvable antiperiodic critical ring (N = 256, Q = 64, ell = 48). [E-num] BINARY CLOCK: the quarter-turn clock is a signed permutation with rho^4 = -1 EXACTLY -- the fermionic mu4 clock is the order-8 double-cover lift (the same Z2-lift pattern as 2I over I). [E-num] EXACT SECTOR DECOUPLING: the primitive-8th-root character projectors resolve the identity and commute with the reduced covariance at 1e-15 (the Rehren-Tedesco diagonal 4-fold-cover isomorphism at covariance level). [E-num] COVER/TWIST: each sector kernel is the single-interval quarter-ring kernel with boundary twist lambda_k; sector spectra union = full spectrum at 1e-14. [E-num] CLOCK INVARIANCE: rho C rho^-1 = C at 1e-14 => [rho, K] = 0 by functional calculus -- omega o rho = omega HOLDS at the 4-interval state level. [E-num] NEGATIVE CONTROL: displacing ONE interval by one site re-couples the sectors at 1e-2 (vs 1e-15). [N] CONJUGATE-POINT MIXING: every cross-interval K row peaks on |s'-s| <= 2 at both sizes -- the lattice shadow of the Casini-Huerta mixing term (band energy spreads with size, honest). [C] continuum multi-interval theory cited; [O] the raw-seam premise (QGEO.SYM.01/SEAM.EQUIV.01) stays open. Numerical (numpy), Python-only by nature."),
    ("v481_seesaw_carrier_ladder", "FLAV.NUSCALE.02: the absolute neutrino-mass scale under the CARRIER Yukawa normalisation y_nu = y_t -- FLAV.NUSCALE.01's two-parameter (y_nu, M_R) trade-off collapses to ONE parameter and the required M_R lands INSIDE the compiler's own PS window; the nearby integer c3-rung is explicitly DECLINED at 1-loop (v354/v355). CANDIDATE class (genre v467/v468); frozen record untouched; no gate closes. [P] CARRIER NORMALISATION (named premise): one SO(10) 16 per family + minimal Yukawa sector (10_H / PS (1,2,2)) => y_nu = y_t at the matching scale -- the trade-off collapses to M_R alone. [N] INVERSION INSIDE THE WINDOW: the observed m_3 = 0.0503 eV demands M_R = 9.3e13 GeV, INSIDE [M_PS, M_GUT] = [4.2e13, 2.4e15] (v249), at log_c3(Mbar/M_R) = 3.15 (y_nu = 1 gives the structureless 2.58 -- the old FLAV.NUSCALE.01 number). [X] INTEGER-RUNG HONESTY GATE: M_R = c3^3 Mbar = 1.53e14 GeV predicts m_3 = 0.030 eV (40% low at 1-loop; ADKLR kappa run-down factor 0.794) -- NEAR the rung (3.15 vs 3), NOT ON: ladder pin DECLINED; the decision computation is named (2-loop SM + explicit PS threshold matching). [N] FALSIFIABLE BAND: over the PS window m_3 spans [0.002, 0.115] eV bracketing the observation; the M_PS end (Sigma ~ 0.124 eV) is already in tension with DESI ~0.072 -- cosmology cuts the window from below; NO floor Sigma = 0.059 eV stays the falsifiable edge (v272). [C]/[O] candidate class; the absolute scale stays formally open. Numerical (explicit 1-loop RG: gauge/y_t/lambda up, ADKLR Weinberg-operator down), Python-only by nature."),
    ("v482_seesaw_rung_decision", "FLAV.NUSCALE.03: the decision computation NAMED by v481, EXECUTED in bracketed (assumption-robust) form -- the integer rung M_R = c3^3 Mbar is EXCLUDED as an unstructured exact pin, conditional on the carrier premise y_nu = y_t; no gate closes. [E-num] THE GAP: central m_3(rung) = 0.0301 eV vs observed 0.0503 -- rescue factor F_req = 1.670 (+67%, 0.154 c3-rungs). [E-num] BRACKETED EXCLUSION: with m_t(MSbar) +-3 GeV (>3 sigma), alpha_3^-1 -+0.10 (>3 sigma), a +-10% band on the ADKLR kappa run-down, and the PS-leg Yukawa beta scaled x[0.5,1.5] between M_PS and M_R, the largest single shift is x1.10 and the ALL-favourable combination reaches only x1.165 -- far below x1.670: the v481 1-loop miss is NOT an RG artifact. [C] NAMED ESCAPE, RECORDED AND DECLINED: only a third-generation Majorana structure factor r ~ 1.67 revives the rung; post-hoc r_needed = 1.6696 sits 0.18% from g_car/N_fam = 5/3 -- no mechanism forces a 3/5 Clebsch on M_R3 today, so this is a named coincidence with a named missing mechanism (PS Majorana-sector Clebsch), declined per v354/v355 (the t0 ~ 30 pattern of v478). [O] the v481 one-parameter window candidate (M_R free in the PS window; NO floor Sigma m_nu = 0.059 eV) never used the integer rung and stands; frozen record untouched. Numerical (explicit 1-loop RG + bracketed envelopes), Python-only by nature."),
    ("v483_pillowcase_exact_traces", "HYP.PHI0.GEOM.01: the GEOMETRIC side of the phi0 puncture target (HYP.PHI0.PUNCTURE.01/v408) is EXACT -- every twisted/orbifold heat trace of the flat tau = i pillowcase is a t-INDEPENDENT RATIONAL -- so the pi^-4 in dtop = 48 c3^4 cannot come from flat orbifold geometry at ANY order; the target NARROWS from 'derive the term' to 'derive the per-mark weight'. [E-num] TWISTED TRACES EXACTLY 1: Tr(gamma e^{t Delta}) = 1 for gamma = sigma (z->-z), rho (z->iz), rho^3 at every tested t in [0.05, 3] (position-space Gaussian image sums / erf closed forms + 2d quadrature, residual < 1e-9; mode-space proof: only n = 0 is gamma-diagonal) -- t-independent, no asymptotic tail. [E] ATIYAH-BOTT MATCH: 1 = 4 x 1/|det(1-dsigma)| (det = 4 = |mu4|) and 1 = 2 x 1/|det(1-drho)| (det = 2 = |Z2|). [E] PILLOWCASE DATA EXACT: orbifold heat trace = (1/2) Tr_T2 + 1/2 (contact term EXACTLY 1/2 = 4 x 1/8 per mark, all t); clock-equivariant trace exactly 1 (all t). [E]/[O] THE REDUCTION: the analytic content of dtop = 48 c3^4 = 3/(256 pi^4) must sit in the per-insertion COUPLING normalisation -- 4 = |mu4| insertions of weight c3 give c3^4, multiplicity Omega_adm = 48; the bare 1/(2 pi)-propagator 4-cycle differs by the exact rational 3/16; the ONE remaining [O] is the rule 'per-mark weight = c3' (seam zeta/Green normalisation, same residual class as EM.WARD.02). HYP.PHI0.PUNCTURE.01 stays open; no gate closes. Numerical verification of exact statements + sympy exact arithmetic; Python-only by nature."),
    ("v484_seam_contact_unit", "SEAM.CONTACT.UNIT.01: the shared rule behind the TWO open analytic targets ALPHA.QUILLEN.EXACT.01 and HYP.PHI0.PUNCTURE.01 is ONE identity -- the seam CONTACT UNIT 'c3 per boundary insertion' -- and it is NOT a new unknown: it is the KMS seam unit 2 pi = 1/(4 c3) with 1/4 = 1/|mu4| (v239), i.e. one bare boundary propagator ORBIT-AVERAGED over the four marks. [E] UNIT CHAIN: 1/(2 pi) = 4 c3 = |mu4| c3 = |Z2| chi(S^2) c3 -- one bare insertion / |mu4| = c3 exactly. [E] MECHANISM DERIVED ON THE SEAM CIRCLE: G(d) = -(1/pi) ln|2 sin(d/2)| (polylog identity, 40 digits); at the mu4 separations G is an INTEGER multiple of c3 ln2 (G(pi/2) = -4 c3 ln2, G(pi) = -8 c3 ln2), so G_marks = -4 c3 ln2 x circ(0,1,2,1), spec = {4,-2,0,-2}; the mu4-invariant (orbit-averaged) insertion carries (GV)|_marks = -(c3 ln2) C exactly -- the log-det contact expansion is EXACTLY graded in c3 per insertion with integer cycle combinatorics Tr(C^k) = 4^k + 2(-2)^k. [E] SUITE-WIDE GRAMMAR: F_U(1) ladder {0,3,6} (v3); phi0 ladder {1,4} (v37); Lambda prefactor 3/(4 pi^2) = (8 pi)^2 delta_top = 48 c3^2 (v60) -- the SAME multiplicity Omega_adm = 48 as the puncture at TWO insertions; the g-2 seam loop divides by the same 2 pi = 1/(4 c3). [C]/[O] THE MERGE: the two tracked [O] targets collapse into ONE named analytic step -- the diagonal (self-energy) zeta-renormalisation at the marks + the state-multiplicity matching (48 = Omega_adm, 41 = 10 b1); the finite cycle sector is proven. Anti-numerology: the integers are forced by the square configuration; no target coefficient is claimed. Exact (sympy + 40-digit mpmath polylog); Python-only by nature."),
    ("v485_contact_diagonal_closed", "SEAM.CONTACT.UNIT.02: the DIAGONAL channel of the merged analytic target (v484) settled at the computable level -- the merged residual COLLAPSES ONTO THE KEYSTONE. [E] DIAGONAL ZERO AT THE KMS SCALE: the renormalised coincident-point Green function on circumference l is G_reg(0; l) = (1/pi) ln(l/2pi) exactly (symbolic limit + 30-digit checks) -- it VANISHES iff l = 2 pi = 1/(4 c3), the v239 KMS seam circumference: the seam scale is the unique zero-self-energy scheme point. [E] THE LOG IS THE SCALE CHANNEL: rescaling gives (1/pi) ln kappa and nothing else -- matching the functional structure (F_U(1) carries exactly ONE log term, the transport 8 b1 c3^6 ln(1/phi_seam); the phi0 split is log-free); [C] reading: log = diagonal/scale channel, log-free = contact data at the KMS point. [E] CLOSED-FORM RESUMMATION (BFK route, v151 class): the finite-rank mark determinant resums exactly, det(I - u C) = (1 - 4u)(1 + 2u)^2 with u = eps c3 ln2 -- all orders; the LINEAR term is absent precisely because the diagonal vanishes (Tr C = 0); series matches v484's Tr(C^k) = 4^k + 2(-2)^k. [E] WEIGHT DICHOTOMY: the SAME 48 = 3 x 16 admissible states carry both multiplicities -- flat count 48 = Omega_adm (phi0 puncture) vs Y^2/loop/GUT-weighted 41 = 10 b1 = 40 + 1 (Tr_16 Y^2 = 10/3 exact, nu^c = 0; Ginsparg (3/5)(41/6) = 41/10, v470) -- one state set, two response weights. [C]/[O] CONSEQUENCE: with v484, EVERY finite/computable piece of the merged ALPHA.QUILLEN + PHI0.PUNCTURE target is proven; the single remaining [O] is the identification of the abstract seam zeta-det with this glued mark determinant -- a face of SEAM.EQUIV.01, exactly the v382 typing, now substantiated computationally. No gate closes, no marker moves. Exact (sympy limits/determinants + 30-digit mpmath + exact Fraction charge sums); Python-only by nature."),
    ("v486_transfer_full_rule", "HYP.REWRITE.02: the FULL physical transfer spectrum {1, (2/3)^6, (1/3)^6} (v54/v221) from ONE forced local rule -- the lazy Z2-pair walk; the (1/3)^6 mode, previously generator-less, gets its local-rule origin; sharpens HYP.REWRITE.01 (v327), whose uniform rule produces {1, 2/3, 0} and can never generate the third mode. [E] UNIQUENESS: for M(s,h) = [[1,0,0],[0,s,h],[0,h,s]] (one absorbing family channel + SYMMETRIC Z2 pair) the survival spectrum is {s+h, s-h}; demanding the physical pair {2/3, 1/3} forces UNIQUELY (stay, hop, leak) = (1/2, 1/6, 1/3) = (1/|Z2|, 1/(|Z2| N_fam), 1/N_fam) -- atom form recorded (honest direction: spectrum -> rates). [E] SIX-HAND GENERATION: over the order-6 = 2 N_fam = |R+(A3)| hand, eig(B^6) = {64/729, 1/729} = {(2/3)^6, (1/3)^6} exactly; decay gaps 6 ln(3/2) (the recovery gap, v76) and 6 ln 3 (the subdominant gap, now generator-full). [E] SUPERSESSION: the uniform rule's zero mode persists under every power -- no iterate reaches (1/3)^6; its lambda_2 arity story (2/3 = |Z2|/N_fam) is unchanged. [E] sub-stochastic, symmetric (detailed balance), absorbing democratic attractor unchanged (v317). [O] the arity {2,3} stays the anchor input; the lazy-vs-uniform split is SELECTED by the physical spectrum, not yet first-principles-derived (named candidate: stay = 1/|Z2| as the sheet-symmetric choice). Exact (sympy); mirrorable, deferred to the next verified Wolfram engine run."),
    ("v487_transfer_clock_rungs", "HYP.REWRITE.03: the lazy split (1/2, 1/6) is FORCED by the resummed clock -- the v486 [O] 'split selection' closes onto v124 structure; sharpens HYP.REWRITE.02, no gate closes. [E] RUNG READING: the lazy rule's one-step spectrum is EXACTLY the complete v124 clock ladder below the wall, eig(M) = {1 - n/3 : n = 0, 1, 2} = {1, 2/3, 1/3}; v327's uniform rule puts its second pair mode ON the wall (0 = 1 - 3/3) -- the v486 degeneracy re-read as 'odd channel collapsed to the wall'. [E] DECK PARITY = RUNG INDEX: [B, sigma] = 0; the sigma-even pair mode carries rung n = 1 (survival 2/3), the sigma-odd mode rung n = 2 (survival 1/3) -- each clock step flips the deck parity; the structural home of the v486 parity assignment (omega_1 even-channel, omega_2 odd-channel) tested by the frb-parity-comb search. [E] FORCING: faithful ladder (no rung missing, no physical mode on the wall -- definitional for a full-spectrum generator) + Z2 equivariance + rates >= 0 force UNIQUELY both the split (1/2, 1/6) AND the assignment even -> rung 1, odd -> rung 2 (the swapped assignment needs h = -1/6 < 0); the 'sheet-symmetric choice' candidate is superseded by this proof. [E] BEND COROLLARY: omega_1/omega_2 = rate(2)/rate(1) = log_{3/2} 3 -- the parity-comb tone ratio IS the v107/v124 bend of the pulsar-clock search. [O] the channel count 3 = N_fam is forced by the clock wall; the ladder stays an [I] identity on frozen spectra (semiclassical derivation R1/[P] open); the arity {2,3} stays the anchor input. Exact (sympy); mirrorable, deferred to the next verified Wolfram engine run."),
    ("v488_majorana_clebsch_door", "FLAV.NUSCALE.04: the 3/5 CLEBSCH DOOR of the seesaw rung, ENUMERATED AND CLOSED -- v482's named escape (a third-generation Majorana factor r ~ 1.6696, 0.18% from g_car/N_fam = 5/3) is decided NEGATIVE at the group-theory level; the v481 window candidate stands as the honest endpoint. [E] NO RENORMALISABLE CHANNEL: sym^2(16) = 136 = 10 + 126; the 126bar is NOT in the E8 hull {1, 10, 16, 45} (v247) -- M_R only via the d=5 operator (16_F 16bar_H)^2/Lambda with the E8-allowed 16_H. [E] CHANNEL LIST: 16 x 16bar = 1 + 45 + 210; the hull admits singlet + 45 insertions (210 absent). [E] CHARGE TABLE: Y = T_3R + (B-L)/2 on all 16 states, Tr_16 Y^2 = 10/3 (v485); (B-L, T_3R, Y)(nu^c) = (+1, -1/2, 0). [E] {2,3}-SMOOTH THEOREM: every nonzero nu^c channel weight {1, 1/4, 1, -1/2, 3/8} is {2,3}-smooth and the multiplicative closure of {2,3}-smooth rationals never contains 5/3; the UNIQUE natural 5 of the embedding, k_Y = Tr Y^2/Tr T_3L^2 = 5/3 (Ginsparg v470), is a full-multiplet trace whose direction has Y(nu^c) = 0 EXACTLY -- structurally decoupled from the Majorana operator. [E] GENERATION-BLINDNESS: the Clebsch is a family-space scalar; diag(1, 1, 3/5) cannot arise from group theory. [O] compiler-flavor inventory typed and declined: exact 3/5's only in wrong slots (K lepton gen2/gen1; R + L lepton gen3/gen2), no degenerate-base shape, no M_R link (v354/v355). Exact (Fraction/sympy); mirrorable, deferred to the next verified Wolfram engine run."),
    ("v489_seam_modular_commutator", "SEAM.CCC.01: the chiral central charge c_- = 8 measured DIRECTLY from the bulk ground state of the v367 seam lattice model, via the Kim-Shehab-Kim modular commutator J(A,B,C) = i Tr(rho_ABC [K_AB, K_BC]) = (pi/3) c_- on a 120-degree pie tripartition -- the FIRST ground-state witness for premise (i) of SEAM.EQUIV.01 (c_- = 8) INDEPENDENT of both the Chern route (v367 FHS curvature) and the counting route (v378 KLM/det-Cartan): J is read off the entanglement data of the exact BdG ground state alone (Peschel covariance, W = -2 artanh Gamma). [E] GROUND-STATE PURITY: eig(i Gamma) = +-1 to 6e-15. [E] PER-LAYER c_- = 1/2: c_- = 0.499998 at L=32, R=12 (0.499793 at L=16 -> 0.500000 at L=48, dev -1.8e-7; tol 1e-4 keeps the suite fast). [E] CONTROLS: trivial M=3 -> 0.000000; orientation flip M=-1 -> -0.499986 (sign flip). [E] LAYER ADDITIVITY EXACT (1.4e-14): J additive over decoupled layers. [E] 16-LAYER CARRIER c_- = 8 = g_car + N_fam: direct 16-layer run 7.9967 (L=16, tol 1e-2; L=24 gives 7.999781), additivity route 8.0000 (tol 1e-3). [E] CLIP INVARIANCE: eps 1e-8 vs 1e-12 moves c_- by 5e-8. [O] HONEST FENCE: pins c_- = 8 on the lattice ground state (third independent witness); does NOT close SEAM.EQUIV.01 -- the continuum scaling limit (MMST v336) stays [O], the mu4 condensation stays the cited KLM step (v378). Numerical (numpy), Python-only by nature."),
    ("v490_seam_parity_census", "SEAM.MU.01: the T^2 spin-structure fermion-parity census for the v367 seam lattice model -- the lattice ground-state witness of 'mu_pre = 4 before condensation' (step 1 of the v378 KLM chain) + the 16-fold-way bridge theta_v = 1 with the MEASURED nu = 2 c_- = 16 (v489). Ground-state parity per boundary-condition sector (AA, AP, PA, PP), determined TWICE: Read-Green TRIM product AND real-space Majorana Pfaffian sign (Schur), relative to the trivial M=3 phase. [E] REAL-SPACE = BLOCH SANITY: twisted spectra match to 9e-15. [E] PER-LAYER CENSUS (+,+,+,-): TRIM == Pfaffian in every sector -- 3 even sectors, the nu = 1 Ising signature. [E] 16 LAYERS => mu_pre = 4: parity^16 = + in ALL 4 sectors => gauged torus GSD = 4 = mu(SO(16)_1) = |det Cartan(D8)|. [E] 16-FOLD-WAY BRIDGE: theta_v = exp(2 pi i nu/16) = 1 EXACTLY at nu = 2 c_- = 16 (vortex bosonic, condensable); rivals nu = 1, 2, 8 excluded (not holomorphically condensable). [E] NON-DISCRIMINATOR FENCE: the fermionic Kitaev-Preskill TEE is identically zero -- gamma_f = 0.000001 (M=1) and 0.000000 (M=3) -- an invertible fermionic phase has no TEE, so gamma_f does NOT discriminate (E8)_1 vs SO(16)_1. [C] KLM step mu_post = 4/2^2 = 1 stays cited (the condensed model is interacting); numerics pin only {c_- = 8, mu_pre = 4, theta_v = 1}. [O] continuum limit (MMST v336); SEAM.EQUIV.01 stays [O]. Python (numpy + scipy Schur + sympy exact theta_v)."),
    ("v491_p2_partition_corollary", "P2.PARTITION.01: g_car = 5 as a COROLLARY of the four marks -- the partition sharpening of v53 (sympy exact, no floats). THE LEMMA: a multiset of exactly 3 POSITIVE INTEGERS summing to 4 is unique -- {1,1,2} -- so e = (e1,e2,e3) = (4,5,2) and g_car = e2 = 5, |Z2| = e3 = 2, N_fam = e2-e3 = 3 are COROLLARIES, not inputs; consistency closes as a fixed point ((2^4-1)/5 = 3 = rank H^1 = #marks-1). NEGATIVE CONTROLS (every assumption load-bearing): drop positivity -> 4 solutions, e2 ambiguous {0,3,4,5}; sum 3 -> e2 = 3; sum 5 -> not unique; 2/4 parts -> e2 {3,4}/{6}; Mehta-Seshadri RATIONAL weights -> e2 = 16/3 resp. 44/9 != 5 (integrality comes from the Birkhoff-Grothendieck SPLITTING-TYPE typing, not from MS weights). [E] v53 SHARPENING: v53 needs all three targets (4,5,2); the partition needs only e1 = 4 -- same unique {1,1,2}. [E] SUM RULE: 4 x (N-1)/2 = 4 iff N = 3; v115 route |a|_1 = |mu4| tr(A0) = 4. INDEPENDENCE CHAIN: #marks = 4 from v216 (P1-side, no g_car); rank H^1 = 3 pure topology (v137/v228); |a|_1 = 4 g_car-free (par-deg-0/(U) v115 or mu4-average). [C] HONEST RESIDUAL: P2 NOT axiom-free -- the weight-TYPING postulate remains (integrality/positivity h^0=0/sum given (U)); AX.P2.01 stays a declared axiom; N_fam direction reversal vs tfpt_constants typed as over-determination, never double-counted. Exact (sympy); Wolfram-mirrored."),
