    ("v585_pnt_locking_split", "PRIME.LOCKSPLIT.01: the two-layer split of the locking cancellation -- THE DOMINANCE IS DENSITY, THE LOCKING IS ARITHMETIC (6 checks, ~3 s; discovery probe pnt_locking_split_probe.py 6/6, verdict TWO-LAYER-SPLIT).  Running the v583 prime-free model through the Paper-II normalised defect delta = det(B-S)/((B-S)_11 (B-S)_22) on all 70 declared windows: [MEASURED, central] the density model misses the real lock by 2-4 orders of magnitude (median ratio 1350, growing h^1.08) -- in stark contrast to det S, which the SAME model reproduces to 1.02-1.14 (v583): the DEPTH of the lock is the primes.  [MEASURED] the one-mode GEOMETRY is density-level: the prime-free pencil also locks its eigenvalue near 1 (coarse lock 1e-2..1e-4) -- the v569 geometry needs no primes.  [MEASURED] the two decay layers: density delta_PNT ~ h^-1.43 (always positive, log-scatter 0.70), real ~ h^-2.51; the arithmetic layer supplies an extra ~ h^-1.08 cancellation ON TOP.  [MEASURED] deep-window overshoot: the real defect goes NEGATIVE exactly at h = 1219, 1445 (plus the 1292 anomaly) while the deterministic model never does -- the sieve horizon is where arithmetic overwhelms density.  [C] BUDGET RELOCATION for Problem 7.1 (target h^-3+eps): density supplies ~ -1.4 deterministically (classical analysis of the closed model), the primes supply the remaining ~ -1.1 (zero-oscillation territory).  Completes the v582/v583 typing.  Surface-ladder measurements; no uniformity, no rate, NO RH statement.  Python-only, counted per GATE.WOLFRAM.02.  Discovery: experiments/tfpt-discovery/pnt_locking_split_probe.py (2026-07-31, 6/6, TWO-LAYER-SPLIT)."),
    ("v586_pnt_lock_direction", "PRIME.LOCKDIR.01: the locking DIRECTION is density-determined -- THE PRIMES ARE A PURE DEPTH AMPLIFIER ALONG A DENSITY-FIXED DIRECTION (7 checks, ~3 s; discovery probe pnt_lock_direction_probe.py 7/7, verdict DIRECTION-DENSITY-FIXED).  [MEASURED, central] the real locking eigenvector of the pencil B^-1 S agrees with the verbatim v583 prime-free model to max 0.331 deg, median 0.030 deg, decaying ~ h^-1.16 on all 69 regular windows -- while the lock DEPTH differs by a median factor 1350 (v585): geometry, spectator separation (v569) and the locking direction are all density-level; only the depth scalar is arithmetic.  [MEASURED, witness] the deterministic direction CERTIFIES the real defect: the quadratic form of the real B-S along the prime-free direction reproduces the true minimal eigenvalue within [0.976, 2.881] (median 1.42) on every window -- the arithmetic content of Problem 7.1 is ONE quadratic form along ONE deterministic vector.  [MEASURED, resolves the v577 puzzle] the deterministic direction itself drifts (v2/v1 from -1.73 to -1.19): the slow v577 angle decay against the fixed null ray (2,-1) was a comparator artifact -- against the correct finite-h deterministic direction the alignment is ~0; the drift limit under 1/log h is -0.551 (R^2 0.67), consistent with the null-ray value -0.5, typed consistent NOT settled.  [E, must-break] scrambled combs misalign by 6.1-25.1 deg (vs 0.026 deg real): the alignment is real placement matching the density profile.  [C] the classical program: prove the deterministic direction/depth asymptotics (closed 1D analysis, no primes), the rest is the depth scalar (zero-oscillation).  Surface measurements; no uniformity, no rate, NO RH statement.  Python-only, counted per GATE.WOLFRAM.02.  Discovery: experiments/tfpt-discovery/pnt_lock_direction_probe.py (2026-07-31, 7/7, DIRECTION-DENSITY-FIXED)."),
    ("v587_w_closed_form", "PRIME.WCLOSED.01: the diagonal companion of the v576 cross formula -- A NEW EXACT FORMULA closes the S-side entries of the deterministic layer (6 checks, ~2 s; discovery probe w_closed_form_probe.py 6/6, verdict CLOSED-FORM-EXACT).  [E, the new exact formula] the diagonal lag weight of the corpus is the SINGLE closed expression W_kk(d) = (2/N)[(N-1-d) cos(w_k d) + sin(w_k(d+1))/sin(w_k)] (d >= 1; W(0) = 1) -- machine-exact (1.9e-15) against v563 lag_weights_from_v for h = 7..1000, modes k = 1..3, ALL lags.  [E] the building blocks are closed Dirichlet sums (ac and the two convolution branches, machine-exact), and the apparent piecewise break at d = m CANCELS on assembly; the reflection-edge suppression is an exact two-term cancellation (both terms O(s) at d = N-1-s).  [E/MEASURED, the payoff] the exact discrete cell-sum S_ij = sum_d lambda(cell) W_ij(d) reproduces the v583 prime-free model: entries to 1.0011-1.0036 and det to 0.9999-1.0003 on h = 184/540/997/1445 -- the S-side of the deterministic layer is CLOSED-FORM (finite geometric-trig sums).  [E] the macro limit is g_k(sigma) = 2(1-sigma)cos(2 pi k sigma) + sin(2 pi k sigma)/(pi k), and the v579 kernel is its edge-anchored version IDENTICALLY (W_inf(sigma) = g(1-sigma)); the elementary Laplace closed forms (rational-exponential in alpha) are the macro limits of the entries.  [C] the classical program of v585/v586 has its first step DONE at the entry level; named next: the arch/B-side closed form, then the delta_PNT(alpha) expansion and the locking-direction drift as explicit expansions.  No uniformity, no rate, NO RH statement.  Python-only, counted per GATE.WOLFRAM.02.  Discovery: experiments/tfpt-discovery/w_closed_form_probe.py (2026-08-01, 6/6, CLOSED-FORM-EXACT)."),
    ("v588_closed_delta", "PRIME.CLOSEDDELTA.01: the deterministic layer of Problem 7.1 in closed form -- BOTH SIDES OF THE DEFECT ARE ONE FUNCTION (6 checks, ~5 s; discovery probe closed_delta_probe.py 6/6, verdict CLOSED-DELTA-EXACT).  [E] the closed geometric-trig sums G_ij(beta) = sum_d e^{-beta d} W_ij(d) (exact finite geometric series over the v587 weight formulas) are machine-exact against direct summation.  [E] the archimedean lag kernel IS the trivial-zero ladder: c_ar(d) = -D f(dD), f(w) = e^{-w/2}/(1-e^{-2w}) = sum_n e^{-(2n+1/2)w} (verified 1.000002 at d = 100; near field d <= 32 = explicit quadrature constants of the closed integrand).  [E/MEASURED] the closed B (ladder + near field) reproduces the corpus B on ALL 70 windows: entries to 2e-5, det B to 6e-5.  [E/MEASURED, central] the closed defect delta~ = det(ladder - pole) matches the deterministic layer (v585) to 0.9999-1.0023 on ALL 70 windows including the deep/anomalous ones; its census decay h^-1.40 reproduces the v585 density layer (-1.43).  [C] THE PICTURE: the deterministic layer is the explicit formula skeleton in closed form -- the POLE term (S side, exponent -D/2) against the GAMMA FACTOR (B side, trivial-zero ladder (2n+1/2)D) inside one exact function; the named remaining step for a theorem is elementary asymptotics of G and the ladder; the arithmetic layer (v585) untouched; no uniformity, no rate, NO RH statement.  Python-only, counted per GATE.WOLFRAM.02.  Discovery: experiments/tfpt-discovery/closed_delta_probe.py (2026-08-01, 6/6, CLOSED-DELTA-EXACT)."),
    ("v589_zero_comb", "PRIME.ZEROCOMB.01: the arithmetic layer IS the zeta-zero comb -- follow-up 3 (the zero-oscillation bound) gets its object identified and its difficulty calibrated honestly (4 checks, ~16 s; discovery probe zero_comb_probe.py 4/4, verdict ZERO-COMB-IDENTIFIED).  [E-level] the residual mass oscillation of the atom table IS the explicit-formula zero comb -4 sum sin(gamma u)/gamma: with the first 200 zeros (damped) the dense-grid correlation is 0.82 with regression slope 1.28 (the truncation deficit), pointwise 1.00 at u = 3 where 200 zeros suffice.  [MEASURED] partial depth recovery: at the smallest window (h = 184, pi/D = 208) the lock ratio improves 176 -> 31 with 200 zeros (factor 5.7), NON-monotone in the truncation (50 zeros: 13) -- honest; the deep windows stay out of reach (h = 540 overshoots to 2646x): the 1e-5-level cancellation demands amplitudes far beyond a 200-zero sum.  [C] THE CALIBRATION: the zero-oscillation bound is now a quantified target -- control sum_gamma sin(gamma u)/gamma at window resolution pi/D with amplitude accuracy set by the lock depth; explicit-formula analytic number theory, named as such; NO bound claimed, no uniformity, NO RH statement; Problem 7.1 untouched.  Python-only, counted per GATE.WOLFRAM.02.  Discovery: experiments/tfpt-discovery/zero_comb_probe.py (2026-08-01, 4/4, ZERO-COMB-IDENTIFIED)."),
    ("v590_involution_existence", "QGEO.INVOL.01: the sheet-involution existence question of GATE.QGEO.01, narrowed to a two-demand selection with UNCONDITIONAL existence (7 checks, <1 s; discovery probe involution_existence_probe.py 7/7, verdict EXISTENCE-UNCONDITIONAL).  [E, rigidity] the integral V-commuting involutions are EXACTLY the spectral sign group (Z/2)^3: all eight sign choices on V's eigenspaces {0,1,2} are integer matrices, genuine involutions, and stabilize the integral order Z<U,V> -- on BOTH twins (nontrivial: generic integral operators do not have integral spectral projectors).  [E, the narrowing chain] the v574 rank theorem kills the trace +1 half (6 -> 3, all of Sigma-signature (1,-1,-1)); the seam-reversal demand S e3 = -e3 narrows 3 -> 2; the zero-mode-fixing demand (+1 on ker V, flip exactly the dynamical sheet pair) singles out S0 = [[1,-1,0],[0,-1,0],[0,0,-1]] UNIQUELY: existence is UNCONDITIONAL (explicit, integral, order-stabilizing, trace -1).  [E, honest scope] the corpus RP reflection Sigma = diag(1,-1,-1) does NOT commute with V -- the sheet involution and the RP reflection are different structures; and the alt twin admits the same classification (the involution does not separate the twins, consistent with v567/v572).  [C] GATE.QGEO.01 relocation: involution existence is DERIVED; the residual freedom is the finite two-demand selection; deriving those demands from mu4/D4/H1 is the remaining open of the gate -- named, not claimed.  Python-only, counted per GATE.WOLFRAM.02.  Discovery: experiments/tfpt-discovery/involution_existence_probe.py (2026-08-01, 7/7, EXISTENCE-UNCONDITIONAL)."),
    ("v591_pole_rank_one", "PRIME.POLERANKONE.01: the pole term is EXACTLY rank-one and the locking direction obeys a closed law (5 checks, ~2 s; discovery probe pole_rank_one_probe.py 5/5, verdict POLE-RANK-ONE).  [E, symbolic] the Laplace denominators factor completely -- D11 = (a^2+4pi^2)^2, D22 = (a^2+16pi^2)^2, D12 = (a^2+4pi^2)(a^2+16pi^2), hence D11 D22 = D12^2 -- and the pole (exponential) part is exactly separable: S^pole = -32 pi^2 a e^a g g^T with g_k = k/(a^2+4pi^2 k^2), det S^pole = 0 IDENTICALLY; the residuals are exponential-free.  [E] THE LOCKING-DIRECTION LAW: v2/v1 = -(a^2+16pi^2)/(2(a^2+4pi^2)), limit EXACTLY -1/2 (the Pythagorean null ray (2,-1)), approach -6pi^2/(a^2+4pi^2).  [MEASURED] the law matches the measured prime-free locking directions to 0.04%-1.4% across the ladder (h = 1445: -1.2248 vs -1.2253), and via v586 (real = prime-free to 0.03 deg) it describes the REAL corpus locking direction.  [C] resolutions: the v577 null-ray conjecture is DERIVED (the a -> infinity limit); the v586 drift is the explicit -6pi^2/(a^2+4pi^2) law; det S, det(B-S) and the h^-1.4 density layer are driven entirely by the corrections to the rank-one pole term -- their formal expansion is the named final step.  No uniformity, no rate, NO RH statement.  Python-only, counted per GATE.WOLFRAM.02.  Discovery: experiments/tfpt-discovery/pole_rank_one_probe.py (2026-08-01, 5/5, POLE-RANK-ONE)."),
    ("v592_continuum_det_law", "PRIME.DETLAW.01: the continuum determinant law -- det S in closed form, one full exponential order suppressed, the dominance growth derived (6 checks, ~2 s; discovery probe continuum_det_law_probe.py 6/6, verdict DET-LAW-DERIVED).  [E, symbolic] det S(a) closed; the e^{2a} coefficient is IDENTICALLY zero (the v591 rank-one cancellation) and the exact leading law is det S ~ 640 pi^2 e^a/a^3 (the e^a term with its exact closed coefficient carries the determinant already at window scales: 0.995-1.0002 at a = 3-10; the leading law converges monotonically, 2.03 -> 1.01 at a = 20 -> 160).  [MEASURED] the REAL dominance P = det S/det B tracks the closed formula with log-log correlation 0.9985 across the ladder -- the closed-form origin of the v570 growth; the finite-N gap is typed (continuum captures 0.19 -> 0.50 of the finite-N determinant, growing as D shrinks: the Euler-Maclaurin/edge layer is the named remaining expansion step).  [MEASURED-conditional] the entry-level arithmetic certificate: |S_real - S_model| entries are bounded by sup|Osc| x TV(read profile) with worst margin 47.6x (rigorous GIVEN the measured oscillation sup = 1.47; the unconditional sup is exactly the zero-oscillation theorem, named).  [C] program status: entry closed forms (v587) + ladder/pole assembly (v588) + rank-one/direction law (v591) + the determinant law and certificates (here); remaining: the finite-N expansion, the zero-oscillation theorem, the OS/RP positivity theorem.  No uniformity, no rate beyond the surface, NO RH statement.  Python-only, counted per GATE.WOLFRAM.02.  Discovery: experiments/tfpt-discovery/continuum_det_law_probe.py (2026-08-01, 6/6, DET-LAW-DERIVED)."),
    ("v593_cutoff_completion", "PRIME.CUTOFF.01: the cutoff completes the closed entries -- the finite-N gap of the continuum determinant (v592: 0.19-0.50) was the integration CUTOFF, not a finite-N mystery (4 checks, ~4 s; discovery probe cutoff_completion_probe.py 4/4, verdict CUTOFF-CLOSES).  [E] the cutoff-corrected entries S_ij(a, sigma0) = -2a int_{sigma0}^1 e^{a sigma} g_ij dsigma are closed elementary forms (same rational-exponential class with e^{a sigma0} boundary terms).  [E/MEASURED] with the cutoff the closed entries match the grid model to 0.7-1.0% and the DETERMINANT to 0.2-1.0% across the ladder; the residual is second-order and shrinks monotonically with h (O(1/N^2) kernel corrections -- the O(1/N) terms cancel exactly in the v587 formula).  [C] THE DENSITY LAYER IS CLOSED END-TO-END: exact weights (v587) -> one-function assembly (v588) -> rank-one + laws (v591/v592) -> cutoff completion; remaining: second-order residual bookkeeping.  No uniformity, no rate, NO RH statement.  Python-only, counted per GATE.WOLFRAM.02.  Discovery: experiments/tfpt-discovery/cutoff_completion_probe.py (2026-08-01, 4/4, CUTOFF-CLOSES)."),
    ("v594_unconditional_cert", "PRIME.UNCONDCERT.01: the entry-level arithmetic layer is bounded UNCONDITIONALLY (5 checks, ~2 s; discovery probe unconditional_cert_probe.py 5/5, verdict UNCONDITIONAL-ENTRY-CERT).  [E] the partial-summation identity mass(u) = 4 sqrt(x) - 2 + 2E(x)/sqrt(x) + int_1^x E(t) t^{-3/2} dt (E = psi - t) is machine-verified on the atom table (residual < 1e-6).  [E, cited] the published unconditional bound |psi(x)-x| < 0.94 sqrt(x) (Buethe 2018, 11 < x <= 1e19, via verified zeros) covers the entire declared surface (x <= e^{12.9}) with worst in-range ratio 0.708 and sixteen orders of margin.  [E] the unconditional sup: |Osc(u)| <= |2+C_th| + 1.88 + |int_1^11|_exact + 0.94(u - log 11) = 17.4 at the deepest read vs measured 1.474 (~12x loose but UNCONDITIONAL).  [E, central] the certificate |S_real - S_model| <= sup x TV holds on every tested window/entry with margin 565x: THE FIRST UNCONDITIONAL STATEMENT OF THE PROGRAM -- the entry-level arithmetic layer needs no conjecture and no runtime zero input.  HONEST SCOPE: the determinant-level lock is NOT reachable by sup x TV majorants (stays the zero-oscillation theorem, v589).  External data: Buethe 2018 (Math. Comp.).  Python-only, counted per GATE.WOLFRAM.02.  Discovery: experiments/tfpt-discovery/unconditional_cert_probe.py (2026-08-01, 5/5, UNCONDITIONAL-ENTRY-CERT)."),
    ("v595_mapping_completion", "PRIME.MAPCLOSE.01: the residual bookkeeping, executed -- the v593 residual was the SIGMA MAPPING, and with the exact dictionary the closed forms match the deterministic model at the identity level (4 checks, ~4 s; discovery probe mapping_completion_probe.py 4/4, verdict MAPPING-CLOSES).  [E] the exact dictionary: sigma = d/N, so the continuum cell sum carries a_eff = ND/2 with limits [u0/(ND), 2 alpha/(ND)] (ND = 2 alpha + O(D) by the window construction -- why the alpha-form carried a first-order residual); the antiderivatives are elementary.  [E/MEASURED] entries AND determinant match the grid model to 1.00000-1.00017 across the ladder (1.00000 at h = 1445).  [E, decomposition] the kernel correction enters at 9e-6 (the genuine O(1/N^2) piece); the v593 residual was carried ENTIRELY by the mapping.  HONEST AMENDMENT: v593 attributed its residual to O(1/N^2) kernel corrections -- wrong attribution (first-order in D through the mapping); the v593 numbers stand, the interpretation is superseded here.  [C] the density layer of Problem 7.1 is a finite set of exact elementary evaluations matching the model to 1e-4 and better; every remaining discrepancy from the REAL data is the arithmetic layer.  The det law is additionally formalized in Lean (det_S_closed, det_denominators_factor).  No uniformity, no rate, NO RH statement.  Python-only, counted per GATE.WOLFRAM.02.  Discovery: experiments/tfpt-discovery/mapping_completion_probe.py (2026-08-01, 4/4, MAPPING-CLOSES)."),
    ("v596_lock_projection", "PRIME.LOCKPROJ.01: the 1D reduction of the arithmetic layer -- along the CLOSED lock direction the zero-side functional cancels the closed density value in a NEAR-IDENTITY (6 checks, ~35 s incl. 400 zetazero evaluations; discovery probe lock_projection_probe.py 6/6, verdict NEAR-IDENTITY-1D).  [E] the projection uses the closed v591 direction (parameter-free); bookkeeping q_real = q_model + Delta q exact; one declared outlier (q_model zero-crossing) excluded by floor.  [MEASURED, central] THE NEAR-IDENTITY: |q_real/q_model| has median 7.7e-4 (min 1.8e-4), decaying ~h^-1.01 -- the prime oscillation integrated against the projected read profile reproduces MINUS the closed density value to ~0.1%: the sharpest 1D statement of the lock.  [MEASURED] the coupling spectrum is COLLECTIVE: max single-zero share 5.9%, 56 zeros for half the mass, heavy zeros 14.1/25.0/30.4/40.9 stable -- equidistribution-flavored, killing single-resonance explanations; the 400-zero truncation does NOT reproduce the layer (wrong magnitude/sign at depth -- the v589 plateau).  [E, must-break] scrambled combs give q_scr/q_model ~ -1200 vs +0.0008 real: six orders of magnitude.  [C] THE FINAL RELOCATION: the arithmetic content of Problem 7.1 is ONE approximate identity per window, sum_gamma c_gamma = -(closed constant)(1 + O(h^-1)), couplings explicit, collective; an equidistribution-type theorem for this family IS the remaining statement; no bound, no uniformity, NO RH.  Python-only, counted per GATE.WOLFRAM.02.  Discovery: experiments/tfpt-discovery/lock_projection_probe.py (2026-08-01, 6/6, NEAR-IDENTITY-1D)."),
