    ("v605_translator", "QGEO.TRANSLATOR.01: the translator round (11 checks, ~11 s; discovery probe translator_probe.py 11/11, verdict TRANSLATOR-LANDED).  [E] T1, THE CENTERPIECE: pulling the corpus RP anti-automorphism theta(X) = Sigma X^T Sigma back along the compiler conjugation and composing with the J-adjoint gives an algebra automorphism phi = Jadj o theta_pull -- and phi is INNER: the intertwiner space is 1-DIMENSIONAL, its generator c is invertible, and phi(A) = c A c^-1 holds EXACTLY -- THE CORPUS RP STRUCTURE IS THE J-ADJOINT COMPOSED WITH THE INNER TWIST BY c: the RP anti-automorphism is fully expressed in curve language (polarization + one explicit element); the normalization 14c is Z[omega]-INTEGRAL (denominator 14 = 2 x 7, the parabolic dimension); honest scope: c is unique up to scale by construction but not Gamma-even and not in the word algebra -- its independent geometric identity is the named open.  [E] T2, THE SEAM-INFINITY BRIDGE: in the Smith coordinates of coker(1 - T_inf) = Z^2 + (Z/3)^3, the seam lift has ZERO free coordinates and torsion coordinates (2,2,0) mod 3 -- the seam line is a NONZERO pure 3-torsion class of the infinity monodromy cokernel.  [E] T3, THE 81 SURVIVES: inside the frame-1 span the order chain O_1 subset (O_joint cap span_1) subset P_1 has indices 3^5 = 243 and 3^4 = 81 -- joining all four frames refines each frame's order by exactly 3^5 and the residual saturation defect is EXACTLY the v566 index 81.  [E] T4: the J_fix duality certified -- C_V^T J_fix = J_fix C_Vdual with explicit integer C_Vdual (char x(x-1)(x-2), dual joint trace 3, char(C_U + C_Vdual) = x(x-2)(x-4)); companion Lean addendum in TfptCarrier/CoverEmbedding.lean (Jfix_symmetric, Jfix_det = 72, CV_dual_certificate, CVdual_cubic, dual_joint_trace; lake build green, 3375 jobs).  GATE.QGEO does not move.  Python-only, counted per GATE.WOLFRAM.02.  Discovery: experiments/tfpt-discovery/translator_probe.py (2026-08-01, 11/11, TRANSLATOR-LANDED)."),
    ("v606_mode_separation", "QGEO.MODESEP.01: the mode-separation round (7 checks, ~2 s; discovery probe mode_separation_probe.py 7/7, verdict MODES-SEPARATED).  [E] M1: ALL THREE eigenlines of the sheet operator V (eigenvalues 0, 1, 2), lifted to the unreduced integral module along the unique intertwiner (1-param, rank 3), have ZERO free part in coker(1 - T_inf) = Z^2 + (Z/3)^3 -- like the seam (v605), the zero mode and the top mode are PURE 3-torsion classes at infinity.  [E] M2, THE SEPARATION: the three classes are PAIRWISE DISTINCT elements of (Z/3)^3 (fixed Smith frame: (2,0,2), (2,2,0), (1,2,0) for V = 0, 1, 2; distinctness is frame-invariant) and none is trivial -- the infinity-cusp torsion is a SELECTION CARRIER that distinguishes the zero mode from the top mode, exactly the separation the real structure could NOT provide (only the seam is R-fixed; the 0/2 lines are neither R-fixed nor R-swapped).  [C, honest] the specific coordinate triples are Smith-frame-dependent; the canonical rule singling out the zero mode's class (the '+1' of the v590 demand) from the structure alone is the named remaining step.  [X, honest negative] M3: the cubic invariant of the translator element -- char(7 Gamma(c) c) = y^3 + 3y^2 + 6y - 1, integer monic, irreducible -- has discriminant -783 = -3^3 x 29, NOT a square: Galois group S_3, not abelian, hence NO cyclotomic-subfield identity for c (Kronecker-Weber); the arithmetic-identity route for c is CLOSED, its geometric identity stays the named open.  GATE.QGEO does not move.  Python-only, counted per GATE.WOLFRAM.02.  Discovery: experiments/tfpt-discovery/mode_separation_probe.py (2026-08-01, 7/7, MODES-SEPARATED)."),
    ("v607_selection_rule", "QGEO.SELRULE.01: the selection rule round (10 checks, ~2 s; discovery probe selection_rule_probe.py 10/10, verdict SELECTION-RULE-LANDED).  [E] S1: the torsion of coker(1 - T_inf) is a genuine F_3 space -- omega-multiplication acts as the IDENTITY ((1-omega) acts as zero) -- and the deck rotation r (commuting with T_inf = r^4) acts F_3-linearly on it.  [E] S2, THE RIGIDITY: the induced r-action is the explicit matrix [[0,1,0],[1,0,2],[2,2,2]] mod 3; its only fixed class is 0, and char mod 3 = (x+1)(x^2+1) with x^2+1 IRREDUCIBLE over F_3 -- the action has EXACTLY ONE projective eigenline (eigenvalue -1), structurally, census-confirmed.  [E] S3, THE LABELING: the unique deck eigenline IS the top-mode class (V = 2); the zero mode and the seam are NOT projectively fixed (neither under r nor r^2) -- with v603/v605 the three modes carry mutually exclusive canonical labels: seam = the R-REAL line, top = the unique DECK-EIGEN torsion class, zero = the only UNLABELED mode.  [C] S4, THE RULE: the two-demand involution S_0 acts as -1 exactly on the two labeled modes and +1 on the unlabeled one -- the v590 zero-mode demand is 'fix the unlabeled mode' and the seam-reversal demand is 'reverse the R-real line': BOTH demands are now expressed through canonical cover structure (typed reading, not a continuum derivation; eigen-ness/uniqueness/distinctness are Smith-frame-invariant).  GATE.QGEO does not move.  Python-only, counted per GATE.WOLFRAM.02.  Discovery: experiments/tfpt-discovery/selection_rule_probe.py (2026-08-01, 10/10, SELECTION-RULE-LANDED)."),
